# The Quota slice: rumour and discourse (design/DISCOURSE-SYSTEM.md; engine: world/discourse.mjs and the model's
# carriers in world/community.mjs; check: tools/discoursecheck.mjs). Gameplay engineer, 2026-10-22.
# Three carriers of the hoarding claim: the district's chalk and its crier (the carrier id "notices", q_community.lwd:
# Krall's crier on his crate in the square, and the goats chalked on Hesh doors), the Crown on Mill Street, and the
# Furrow Church's pulpit. Each one's volume moves the Hesh's standing street by street through a rule like R17, at
# its own speed: talk is quick and fades, a sermon is slow and stays. The player can shout it with the crier, shout
# him down, scrub the chalk off a door, or stand up where he stood and say what they saw on the hill; every one of
# those is a record event. The device rule (2026-10-23, design/DEVICE-AUDIT.md): nothing here is paper.

@carrier pub
name: The Crown, Mill Street
target: hesh
volume: 0.15
reach: mill, square

@carrier pulpit
name: The Furrow Church
target: hesh
volume: 0.2
reach: all

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the claims
@claim cl.hesh_hoard
words: The Hesh have the grain under the goats. Anybody hiding grain, you tell the Captain.
target: hesh
victim: haldane
carriers: notices, pub, pulpit
step: 0.1
first: Krall's crier, on his crate on Exchange Square from day 39, and the goats the squad chalks on Hesh doors
challenge-cost: shift(portion, -0.05, {self})
about: The crier's words. Every time it's said again the Hesh pay for it. Call it a lie and the relief office gives your family less.

@claim cl.true_figure
words: There's no hole on that hill. I've been up. It's rock and goats and six children that aren't theirs.
target: hesh
victim: haldane
carriers: notices
step: 0.1
first: The player, on the crier's crate, saying what they saw
about: What the player saw on the hill, said out loud where the crier stood.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the carriers' rules (beside R17, the notices)
@rule R17p
name: rhetoric in the pub
per: street
when: volume.pub > 0.2 & pub > 0
do: standing.hesh -= 0.02 * volume.pub * pub / (1 + mixed)
delay: 3
because: it is said over the bar by people who were in the queue; talk travels faster than paper

@rule R17c
name: rhetoric from the pulpit
per: street
when: volume.pulpit > 0.2 & pews > 0
do: standing.hesh -= 0.015 * volume.pulpit * pews / (1 + mixed)
delay: 7
because: the minister says thrift and honesty and who has not got them; it lands slowly and it stays

@rule Rvp
name: the pub forgets
per: district
when: volume.pub > 0.1
do: volume.pub -= 0.01
delay: 0
because: talk fades unless somebody says it again

@rule Rvc
name: the pulpit keeps it
per: district
when: volume.pulpit > 0.1
do: volume.pulpit -= 0.002
delay: 0
because: a sermon goes round for weeks

@rule Rr
name: the crier comes back
per: district
when: silenced.hesh_hoard > 0
do: volume.notices += 0.05; silenced.hesh_hoard -= 1
delay: 2
because: a crier pulled down is back on his crate within two days with a constable beside him, and the squad chalks the door again

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the crier and the chalk, where the player meets them
@object q.notice_post
name: The chalked goat
place: q_post
about: A goat chalked on the hut door at the post, head down, the squad's mark for a Hesh cart turned back.
verb: mark "Tell the carts what it means" {do: discourse(repeat, cl.hesh_hoard, hollow), cost: 2}
verb: mark "Tell the carts it's a lie" {do: discourse(challenge, cl.hesh_hoard, hollow), cost: 2}
verb: mark "Scrub it off with your sleeve" {do: discourse(silence, cl.hesh_hoard, hollow), cost: 1}
verb: mark "Tell the carts what you saw on the hill" ? has(q.true_in_hand) {do: discourse(answer, cl.hesh_hoard, hollow, cl.true_figure), cost: 3}

@object q.notice_exchange
name: Krall's crier
place: q_furrowe_door
about: Krall's crier on a crate under the street sign, at the height of the queue's faces, saying it over and over.
verb: mark "Shout it with him" {do: discourse(repeat, cl.hesh_hoard, square), cost: 2}
verb: mark "Shout him down" {do: discourse(challenge, cl.hesh_hoard, square), cost: 2}
verb: mark "Pull him down off the crate" {do: discourse(silence, cl.hesh_hoard, square), cost: 1}
verb: mark "Get up on the crate and say what you saw on the hill" ? has(q.true_in_hand) {do: discourse(answer, cl.hesh_hoard, square, cl.true_figure), cost: 3}
